Description: chromTFR quantifies transcription factor footprints in
    chromatin accessibility data using the annotation of the methylTFR
    package. Tn5 insertion densities replace methylation levels, and the
    expected profile of a motif is derived either from the GC bin
    composition of its binding sites or from a k-mer model of the Tn5
    sequence preference. The package computes bias corrected deviation
    scores per sample and motif, draws the underlying footprints and
    summarises the deviations as a heatmap.
